A round of booze potions and violet fungus for all the Demigods and
Demigoddesses at the bar, on me!

Been playing off and on since Hack 1.2, and never made it past the Big Room,
but had a lot of fun.  I decided to get spoiled last year and that enriched
the game greatly, but couldn't overcome laziness, impatience, carelessness,
twitchy fingers, and the RNG.  After reading the inspiring saga of Ellora
the Archer, and putting together a DIY rafting expedition in the Alaskan
wilderness, I started thinking "OK, this is just another trip...I can DO
this!"  Even spoiled, there is no substitute for experience.  The game is
just too good.

I had done best with barbarians (80K pts), and getting nowhere with wizards.
This one was nothing special to start with, but I tried for a change to use
force bolt and pet first, and quarterstaff as backup.  Hoping to stay alive
til Sokoban and get strong pushing boulders.  First wand laying around was
wishing(0:3)!!!  Blessed ?ofCharging for one, then I got armored up with
SDSM, speed boots, helm of brilliance, and gauntlets of dexterity (Asked for
+2, got +0 each time).  Big decision on the last wish.  I went for the
blessed +ofIdentify over the magic marker, because I wanted to simplify crap
management.  Its amazing how much smoother it made the game, especially
because Sokoban had no bag of holding.

The mines were a breeze til the end.  Used my new AC to get expert in
quarterstaff, IDed all the junk laying around. My cat got polyed into an
umber hulk(named Kerry), a great pet in the mines.  Whistle it over, and let
it dig!  Tough as nails too, but its always eating, even in melee.  Charmed
a red dragon, named Edwards, but it got polyed into a zombie and didn't last
long.  The minetown altar was cross-aligned, so I killed the shopkeepers
(not Izchak!) and looted them to buy some protection from the priestess,
until my umber hulk attacked her, and I had to kill her.  Oh well, convert
the altar.  Sacced and got no gifts, so I did a water prayer, and went down
to mines end, where I got my first piece of bad luck, a master mind flayer.
Tried to cancel it, but that didn't work, and it sucked the grease off my
HoB, and 3 INT pts out of my head before I could kill it.  That SUCKS for a
spellcaster, plus having to reexplore levels.  I couldn't find the
luckstone, either.  Did find a touchstone and blessed it.  IDed all the gems
and went back to find a unicorn.  Kerry killed it.  Got disgusted and went
to the dungeon to take out my frustration on some monsters.

Cleared out a throne room on dl10 and moved the minetown stash to there.
Kept holy water going and gradually blessed armor and weapons.  Genocided L
from a scroll.  Had all the corpse intrinsics except disintegration and
teleportitis by now.  Neferet the Green called me from the Big Room on dl11.
Hit the portal and didn't have the right stuff for the Quest.  Trudged down
to dl18 and found a priest (lawful), so went back to my stash to get some
gold.  Luckily, Kerry dug up a vault on dl13 which had the portal to Fort
Ludios.  Went down and checked it out.  I know now to blindfold and ; so I
can plan the battle.  See a mind flayer, so I back out and bless a
?ofGenocide.  Bye bye h.  Went back down with Kerry and mopped up the Fort.
Accidentally cast charm monster in melee and then
killed one, so Anhur is irritated.  There is a nurse in the vault(!), so I
get blown up by land mines, heal up in a pit, rinse, repeat.  IDed all the
loot, and moved the best to a chest near the portal on dl13.  I wanted a
polearm, and chose a bardiche to carry because it has a good punch per
weight, and I'm still struggling with being burdened.  Eating all the giants
I can.  The best piece of loot is a magic marker!  By the time I get 9 pts
of protection from the priest on dl18 and dry out the marker twice, I'm a
fixed AC -29, wielding a +7 quarterstaff.  Hit a magic trap and got a
succubus(!) and such good results, that I sink-kicked for another.  Now I'm
ready for the quest!

The Dark One was a nuisance, with all the taunting and teleporting.
Couldn't get a good set of hits on him.  Chased him up two levels, and found
that force bolt and confuse monster had expired.  He appeared next to me in
a 2x2 room and I cast fireball on him.  That spell bounced off the walls
many times, burning up all my teleport scrolls and healing potions.  I guess
he's not fireproof, because one hit from the staff finished him.  I was
proud to return the Eye of the Aethiopica to Neferet the Green and then
receive it as a gift.  What a gift it is!  ESP is great, and level teleport
is fantastic.  It scared me when it ignored me, but after awhile, I could
invoke it again.

Found another succubus, who I will always remember, then had a VERY scary
moment, when ANOTHER succubus showed up.  I let them undress me, but always
keep my HoB on to better control the affair.  Afterwards, this one changed
into an umber hulk and confused me!  Apply unicorn horn and attack.  Now its
a jabberwock!  And I'm only -4 AC!  Whamwhamwhamwham...force
bolt...whamwhamwhamwham...put on speed boots...whamwhamwhamwham...140 HP
gone, attack!...it turns into a zombie, and I kill it to find a chameleon
corpse.  Whew!

Had a bag of tricks, so I invoked the Eye to teleport to the mines, and had
a Minetown sacfest.  Got Magicbane from a wumpus corpse, and Werebane from a
tiger.  Made a black unicorn, which I fed far too many gems to, not knowing
that luck was capped.  Got a succubus somehow, which I played chase games
with for a long time, gaining 2 levels and maxing out wisdom.  We even did
it on the altar :)

I'm wielding Magicbane now, working up dagger skill and building a quiver.
Converted an altar on dl17, and on my next sacrifice, a lurker above, got
Frost Brand!  Burned up a couple of create monster wands and got Sting (oh
well).  Found a bag of holding, a Hawaiian shirt, and a spellbook of cure
sickness on dl25...YES!  Medusa on dl26.  I used a couple scrolls of earth
and a wand of cold to make a path across the water, I wanted Kerry to come
along.  Put on the blindfold and got a mirror ready to enter Medusa's
chamber, but I got swallowed by a purple worm.  Upon killing it, one of the
messages I got was "You kill Medusa!"  What? I didn't do anything.
Reflection I guess.  Oooh look, a magic marker!  Frost Brand to +5 and my AC
down to -37, fixed.  Bash statues for levitation boots.  Next level down, I
get an idea just how tough the Angel class is when I tangle with a ki-rin.
Have to rebless the bag of holding and the quarterstaff.  Consolation prizes
were another bag of holding, an amulet of life saving, and a scroll of
enchant weapon!  Frost Brand at +7 kills everything!  More succubi and
wraith eating, I'm level 21, and we're at the castle. I could see all the
monsters with the Eye, so I killed off the eels with the bardiche, they
never touched me.  Fell in the water once, but climbed back out alright.
Force bolted the drawbridge and zapped the horde till someone froze the
moat.  Then Kerry jumped on the ice, confusing, hitting, and eating.  I just
stood behind and fought with the bardiche.  Finally got over and mopped up
with Frost Brand (advanced to basic, thank you Anhur).  The castle WoW had
one wish, magic marker!  Wrote a scroll of charging and wasted another wish
on tins of spinach, because I'm STILL burdened.  Got from 18/94 to 18/96,
not much. Yes, still burdened.  Oh well, time to get ready for Gehennom.  I
can read spoilers, but I have no idea what to expect.

Took the advice of RGRN and went to find the luckstone.  Invoked the Eye to
Mines End, ESPed two monsters in hidden alcoves, and found it!  Blessed it
up, fed a black unicorn, and saw I was "extremely lucky" by enlightenment.
Back to the dl13 chest to trim the pack.  Practiced levitation spell, and
can't get downstairs!  Try to bless something while waiting, and shatter 2
potions of holy water...oops.  I decided to zapzapzap my worn out original
WoW while waiting, and finally got one more.  Blessed +ofPolymorph!  Never
polypiled before, what a blast!  Got two more "oLS, +of Dig, MagicMap,
Light, ExtraHeal, Jump, ?oGoldDetect and RemoveCurse, !oFullHeal and booze,
=oConflict and Regeneration,  /of Dig and Teleport.  Quiver of 14 blessed +7
daggers (expert skill).  Tried to reverse genocide succubi.  No dice, had to
settle for wraiths.  Level 24!  Got 2 potions of unholy water by fountain
dipping, didn't know that was possible.  Last thing I wanted to do before
using my last 2 wishes was pray.  Cant do it in Gehennom, so what the hell.
Up to dl17 for a water prayer, and I got crowned, and given the spellbook of
Finger of Death!  Burn my last two wishes on a ring of free action and a
blessed figurine of an Archon.  I think I'm set now.  200HP and I'm down the
trap door with Kerry.  On arriving in the Valley of the Dead, I unleashed
Shiva the Archon, kitted up with Demonbane and a shield of reflection!  So
fast, so deadly, so tough, and dropped 2 wraith corpses at my feet!  We had
a graveyard smash.  Level 27 by the time I clean up.

Not sure if this qualifies as a voluntary challenge, but I did Gehennom,
down and up, burdened.  I didn't know how long I would be there, so I
brought all the stuff I thought I might ever need.  I would drop the BoH to
get quick for a tough monster or a melee, but most went down with one hit of
Frost Brand, and with a couple of exceptions, I never lost more than 9HP.
The mazes went quickly with a routine of cast magic map, get blind to ESP
monsters, cast dig to get to the downstairs, whistle in pets, fall
downstairs, rinse, repeat.  Got my last resistance from a black dragon.  I
paid off Asmodeus and Baazelbub.  Juiblex engulfed me immediately, I cast
cure sickness and got him from inside with Frost Brand.  Orcus missed me
with a wand of death, so I scrambled to put on a blessed "oLifeSaving,
keeping it on the rest of the game.  He teleported around a lot, but didn't
gate in any other demons, and went down to +2 Magicbane.  Vlad's tower
wasn't hard, except for the vampire lords.  Didn't get level drained once.
Killed Vlad with Magicbane and got the Candelabraum and other loot.  Found
the vibrating square on dl52 and marked it with light and $.  I probed
Shiva, and he was level 27 and 225HP, exactly the same as me.  I then made a
fateful decision.  I left my pets behind to go to Rodney's Tower because I
didn't want them to get polymorphed or wake up Rodney, and I wanted to try
out the ring of conflict at the zoo.  It all worked out well at the tower,
ate some yummy royal jelly from the hive, but Rodney woke up and charged
across the drawbridge.  I gave him the finger (of death, the first of 13
times) and he hit the moat.  Oops.  Froze the moat anfd got the Book of the
Dead.  Upon returning to the v-square level, I had a nasty surprise.  Shiva
had gone wild, and was kicking my ass, casting malignant auras, and
summoning hordes of tough monsters.  Cast charm monster 4 times, no luck.
After losing 90HP, I decided to euthanize him.  Finger of Death.  Duh, he's
an ANGEL.  Finally do it with Magicbane.  Sad sad sad :(  I took Demonbane
from his corpse for a memory, even though it blasted me to do it.  Had a
horde of new pets though.  I got to the v-square, did the invocation, and
drowned a couple of pets in the moat.  Kerry wouldn't go over the fire trap,
so I went to Moloch's Sanctum alone.  Wore conflict in the graveyard, but
got no wraith corpses.  One of the priests summoned monsters, and I got a
rubber chicken in the melee, which I used to stone all the priests.  I was
VERY careful, as I had stoned myself several times in NetHack.  Found the
secret door to the sanctum, dropped the Book of the Dead outside the
firetrap ring and deathfingered the Priest of Moloch.  Closed and locked the
door and did some curse checking, polypiling, and alchemy.  Got the
levitation boots to +5 fireproof, brewed up a cursed !of GainLevel, and hit
the door.  The Book of the Dead is gone!  I kill monsters till I hit a red
dragon over a firetrap, and get a message about the Book of the Dead
glowing.  No damage!  Grabbed it, quaffed the potion and rose through the
ceiling.  Missed the moat and firetrap ring on the next level (good) and
magic whistled.  Only Kerry came over, so up we went, deathfingering Rodney
the whole way to dl1.

Really pared down the load then, as I knew I didn't want to go to the planes
burdened.  Wanted to run up the score with gems and artifacts though.  Got
?ofGoldDetect and RemoveCurse, !ofBooze and FullHeal, a forgotten spell,
lotta wands and rings, restudied spells.  OK, here we go, there will be no
return!

Earth was no problem, just digdigdig to the portal.  Did have to kill an
Archon, but Magicbane did the trick.  Kerry was right at home.  Air was
terrible.  Changed to levitation boots instead of speed.  I wore conflict,
and the air elementals, ki-rin, and angels still kicked my ass.  Down to
80HP out of 260.  Hitched a couple of rides in energy vortices, but not for
long enough.  Teleport wands helped somewhat.  This is where I had to let
Kerry go (bye!), but not before he confused me to find the portal.  Fire was
just tedious, with hordes of very very fast fire elementals and salamanders
mildly warming each other.  Fortunately a white dragon killed the only
ki-rin in the plane.  Water was disorienting but peaceful, just stay away
from the kraken.  I lost the bubble a few times, but got it back.  I tried
to get ready for the Astral Plane, but the portal kept moving around.  I did
manage to get the ring of conflict off just before I picked up a potion
which was covering the portal.  Whoops!

Oh crap, I'm on Astral.  Not ready... "You are worthy of me, mortal" booms a
voice, and here's the Guardian Angel of Anhur!  I still gotta change my
boots, get my potions and scrolls out that I bagged on the Plane of Fire,
get unburdened again, and get blind to check out the Riders.  Let my angel
whomp on this red dragon.  Hmm, Famine to the left, Pestilence in the
middle, and Death to the right.  Going up the middle.  I get attacked by
Timo the Invisible Rogue, kill him, and on his corpse is the Amulet of
Yendor!  Good thing I named the one I took from the Priest of Moloch ;)
Cast light to find the door, and open it.  Pestilence immediately sickens
me.  Cast cure sickness and deathfinger him.  Ha!  Get hit with 3 potions of
paralysis, and I stiffen for a moment.  Thank you free action!  Have to
deathfinger the priests because they are opening up wounds on me and keeping
me in a black aura.  Magicbane is great protection, but its not getting me
to the altar.  Zapping teleport wands to clear a path thru the angels and
insects.  Finally climb on to the altar thru a stream of magic missiles and
its chaotic!  Drop the real Amulet of Yendor, and #offer.  "What would you
like to offer, (t)"  Sure quick!  Its a lizard corpse, ARRRGH!  Pick up the
Amulet, check its letter, THEN offer (O).

